  "command": "LEAN_BRIDGE_LAKE_RUNTIME_ROOT='/app/build/lean-link-spike/lazy' LEAN_BRIDGE_LEAN_PREFIX='/app/.toolchains/elan/toolchains/leanprover--lean4---v4.32.2' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_SUBTYPE_BROWSER_TEST='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_SUBTYPE_NPM_MODES='full' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_SUBTYPE_NPM_OUTPUT='/app/build/vo1468-browser-installed-ordinary-full-r1-2f723c1/records' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_SUBTYPE_NPM_ROUTES='ordinary' LEAN_BRIDGE_NOMINAL_SUBTYPE_NPM_TEST='1' LEAN_BRIDGE_TYPE_CORPUS_BROWSERS='chromium,firefox,webkit' LEAN_NUM_THREADS='1' MAKEFLAGS='-j1' NO_COLOR='1' OMP_NUM_THREADS='1' PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH='/app/.toolchains/playwright' '/usr/bin/nice' '-n' '19' '/usr/bin/ionice' '-c' '3' '/usr/bin/taskset' '-c' '3' '/usr/bin/node' '--max-old-space-size=3072' '--test' '--test-concurrency=1' '--test-reporter=tap' 'tests/helpers/nominal-subtype-npm-installed-tests.mjs'",
  "scope": "Both independently built component and shared-runtime npm archives reproduce. Offline installation follows author-root removal. The original strict-TypeScript and Node callers pass before and after moving the installation. Each page, React production/strict and dedicated-worker selection executes in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit: twelve browser executions and 51 lifecycle observations per source/API selection. Checks include missing-asset recovery, React remount and pending-unmount, worker restart and disposal, complete installed-file closure and independently authenticated served Wasm. The full API checks per-use constructor selection and normalization, repeated record fields, active variant branches, aliases, mixed Fin guards, rejection paths, unchanged caller inputs and recovery. Nominal browser acceptance covers the tested Nat records, variants, aliases, nested copied containers and constructor-free results on Linux x64 with Chromium 151.0.7922.34, Firefox 153.0 and WebKit 26.5. Strict TypeScript and Node 22.23.2 callers also pass before and after installation-tree relocation. Two independent author roots reproduce both npm archives; author roots are removed before offline installation. Browser callers use source-free production bundles. Complete component and shared-runtime npm archives, original caller and compiler records, launcher and test output are retained; browser binaries, framework archives and deployment bundles are not. The local compiler ran through the recorded Nix command transport adapter, not a Nix sandbox. Other primitive-base nominal fixtures, refined callbacks, owned, recursive, dependent and broader generic Subtypes remain separate work. Entry counts and memory are unmeasured. These local results do not claim hosted acceptance of a later revision. Historical absolute command paths document the original machine and are not CI prerequisites.",
